{"id": "swebq0189", "pool": "swebq", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 2303132607, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "8c3af78f4533df26d66383d6216ec5cacb9faa8bb324f3d6a6d51641beeea3a9", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "what to see near grand canyon?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/swebq0189.wav", "input_sha256": "96d07f9e9415767d55909cacacba16a7dd5f9cbd07e137d29405ddb22a653202", "input_samples": 40849, "input_s": 2.553, "n_real_chunks": 3, "score": 0.642, "act": 0.9954, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "If you mean near the Grand Canyon South Rim — the most common area to visit — here are the best things to see: Mather Point – classic first Grand Canyon viewpoint near the Visitor Center. , Yavapai Point & Geology Museum – great views plus easy geology exhibits. , Grand Canyon Village – historic lodges, El Tovar, Hopi House, train depot, rim walks. , Hermit Road viewpoints – especially Hopi.", "expert_answer": "If you mean **near the Grand Canyon South Rim** — the most common area to visit — here are the best things to see:\n\n1. **Mather Point** – classic first Grand Canyon viewpoint near the Visitor Center.\n2. **Yavapai Point & Geology Museum** – great views plus easy geology exhibits.\n3. **Grand Canyon Village** – historic lodges, El Tovar, Hopi House, train depot, rim walks.\n4. **Hermit Road viewpoints** – especially **Hopi Point**, **Mohave Point**, and **Pima Point** for sunset views.\n5. **Desert View Drive** – a scenic 23-mile drive east of Grand Canyon Village with multiple overlooks. ([nps.gov](https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/desert-view-drive.htm?tblci=GiDYnKgdf9cNYDLJzSloHDSri9WmiBuewXEdDQfm4-afziDr_kQosduI_qHNqrnVATDRk20&utm_source=openai))\n6. **Desert View Watchtower** – one of the best South Rim viewpoints, near the park’s East Entrance. ([home.nps.gov](https://home.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/desert-view.htm?utm_source=openai))\n7. **South Kaibab Trail** – hike just to **Ooh Aah Point** for a short but dramatic below-rim experience.\n8. **Bright Angel Trail** – iconic trail starting in Grand Canyon Village; even a short walk down is memorable.\n9. **Tusayan** – small gateway town just outside the South Entrance with food, hotels, IMAX, and tours.\n10. **Cameron Trading Post** – good stop east of the park for Native art, food, and souvenirs.\n\nIf you have more time nearby:\n- **Horseshoe Bend** and **Antelope Canyon** near Page, AZ — about 2.5 hours from the South Rim.\n- **Flagstaff** — about 1.5 hours away; good base with restaurants and Route 66 charm.\n- **Sedona** — about 2–2.5 hours away; red rocks, hikes, scenic drives.\n\nNote: the **South Rim is open year-round**, while the **North Rim is more seasonal and remote**, so check conditions if heading there. ([nps.gov](https://www.nps.gov/grca/planyourvisit/index.htm?sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwi4y_Lnw9qBAxUJWqsCHYGlEosQyK4DegQIAxAp&utm_source=openai))", "transcript": "What to see near Grand Canyon.\n", "asr_s": 0.67, "expert_s": 10.55, "expert_input_samples": 40849, "expert_input_s": 2.553, "expert_input_sha256": "96d07f9e9415767d55909cacacba16a7dd5f9cbd07e137d29405ddb22a653202", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 10.881, "relay_synth_ms": 11090, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": false, "n_speak_chunks": 0, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0189_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "6e972327e107c961c0c60216a29322ed32f590175786bc585bf8737f5a69aec7", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 25.8}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/swebq/audio/swebq0189_aggressive_candidate.wav", "sha256": "893627be4a40cc6591f6a437bbebcfcdf67b53272d9950678c85829bf6081370", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 1.0}, "stall": {"path": "/data/ttfa_rea